        ]
      },
      {
        "w": "definitely",
        "pos": "adv.",
        "zh": "一定；肯定",
        "ipa": "/ˈdefɪnətli/",
        "ex": "Definitely means “for sure” or “without doubt.” Alberto says not to look, then says you should definitely look.",
        "exs": [
          "You should definitely see the town above the water."
        ],
        "note": "Day 5 原句：“Don't look at it. Just kidding. Definitely look at it.”（别看。开玩笑的。一定要看）",
        "si": 5,
        "a": [
          "audio/luca_wv/d05_w03.mp3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "w": "collecting",
        "pos": "v.（-ing）",
        "zh": "收集；一直在收集",
        "ipa": "/kəˈlektɪŋ/",
        "ex": "Collecting means gathering things you want to keep. “I've been collecting” means this started in the past and is still true.",
        "exs": [
          "She has been collecting shells since she was small."
        ],
        "note": "Day 5 原句：“As you can see, I've been collecting for a long time, so ask me anything.”（你看，我收集很久了，随便问）",
        "si": 7,
        "a": [
          "audio/luca_wv/d05_w04.mp3"
        ]
      },
      {
        "w": "unfortunately",
        "pos": "adv.",
        "zh": "可惜；不幸的是",
        "ipa": "/ʌnˈfɔːrtʃənətli/",
        "ex": "Unfortunately means “it is sad, but true.” It tells you the next fact is bad news.",
        "exs": [
          "The boat is fast. Unfortunately, it is also loud."
